## Build 3e: reach warm lnlike <= 10 ms on the crown microlensing config by fixing the beat-oscillation problem one layer down, as the owner ruled. Build 3d proved no spline over the CURRENT transition-band channel kernels reaches 10 ms (beats force 50-90 nodes). The fix re-expresses the kernels as smooth ENVELOPES x ANALYTIC CARRIERS: K_a(w) = S(w)*R_a(w) + (1-S(w))*(1/alpha_a)*sum_j alpha_j*R_j(w)*exp(-i*w*Delta_{a,j}), where the per-image residuals R_j are Fresnel-scale smooth, S is the analytic smootherstep, and Delta_{a,j}=tau_j-tau_a are exact geometric delays. Only the envelopes are interpolated (config-independent node count); carriers + smootherstep are applied analytically at dense frequencies. CRITICAL efficiency finding (Professor, code-pinned): the R_j are already produced by the cheap numba _dd/_hyp1f1 special-function path (~1us/image/node), NOT the F_op_grid operator path (0.37ms/node) the brief's pessimistic budget assumed -- so envelopes ALONE project to ~3-5 ms warm, comfortably under the 10 ms gate. Scope: WP1 exposes a thin `transition_envelopes(w)` public method on ChangRefsdalChannels; WP2 rewires `_amplification_coefficients` to interpolate envelopes and reconstruct K_a (same return signature; _data_term/_norm_term/(k0,k1) reduction untouched). Per the Simplifier and the owner's step rule, the micro-levers are DEFERRED as named residual levers rather than shipped: WP3 geometry Newton shortcut (~1.6 ms, but not the bottleneck and the highest-correctness-risk geometry site) and WP4 operator contraction fusion (~1 ms, but touches the F005-certified byte-unchanged refusal path) are both unnecessary to make the ceiling; the 3D surrogate table is likewise deferred (no gitignored-cache/DATA_CONTRACTS complexity this build). KEY CORRECTNESS RISK, carried by the tests and the step rule: whether the per-image _dd residual reconstruction reproduces exact_total across the FULL transition band including deep-unresolved near-caustic sub-bands (near-cusp/near-fold anchors). The Professor found no obstruction, but the binding gate is reconstruction-vs-exact_total at the 1e-3 null-safe production gate across all five anchor configs; if any sub-band fails, gate at the derived floor, name the residual, and escalate the sub-band to the owner -- do NOT widen tolerances. Timing gates are self-relative and arithmetic-derived (the 41ms/18.8ms cross-harness discrepancy is unresolved): structural-first (node-count config-independence across the five anchors; public-entry-point speedup floor vs brute), then a warm best-of-5 pinned <=10 ms ceiling measured in one self-consistent harness. No DATA_CONTRACTS artifact is produced or consumed (surrogate deferred), so no producer->consumer ordering applies. Assumption: envelope node base fixed at a config-independent _ENVELOPE_NODES=48 (Professor's conservative Fresnel bound), unioned with the existing F008 regime-boundary frequencies. NOTE: Serena memory tools were unavailable this session, so the architect_short_term checkpoint could not be written (fallback: the Professor persisted the design into professor_short_term and professor_code_observations).

### WP1: Expose smooth per-image envelopes from the Chang-Refsdal engine
  What: Add a public method `transition_envelopes(w)` to `ChangRefsdalChannels` that returns, per coarse w-node, the SMOOTH per-image diffraction residuals R_j(w), the magnification amplitudes alpha_j, the per-image gauge delays tau_j, and the minimum full-cluster pairwise delay separation delay_sep (the smootherstep scale). No behaviour change to any existing method; no change to _gauge.py, operator.py, _dd.py, or _hyp1f1.py.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/channels.py
  How: Loop over images j calling the EXISTING `image_amplification_factor(w, j)` then `_kernel_from_image_amplification(F_j, j)`; domain analysis confirmed the latter returns R_j = F_j/(alpha_j*exp(-i*w*tau_j)) -- the smooth Fresnel-scale residual computed via the numba _dd/_hyp1f1 path (~1us/image/node), NOT F_op_grid. Assemble R as an ndarray of shape (n_images, len(w)); return the tuple (R, alpha, tau, delay_sep). alpha and tau are the per-image gauge constants already held on the instance; delay_sep is the minimum pairwise |tau_j - tau_k| over the FULL cluster -- reuse the existing full-cluster neighbour computation (`_min_delay_separation` / the F008 real+parked-virtual set); do NOT reintroduce a real-only neighbour set (F008). Document the valid domain in the docstring: R_j is returned on the full node grid and regime weighting is the caller's responsibility via the analytic smootherstep S(w); this method does not gate on regime. Preserve refusal semantics: if any per-image evaluation raises geometry.LensDomainError or operator.CancellationError, let it propagate unswallowed. Keep the method a thin wrapper -- no interpolation or reconstruction logic here. Do NOT alter _channel_switch, _exact_kernel_resolved/_unresolved, exact_total/_exact_total, or any refusal threshold.
  Who: Coder
  Verification: `ChangRefsdalChannels.transition_envelopes(w)` exists and returns (R with shape (n_images,len(w)), alpha, tau, delay_sep), R being the smooth per-image residuals sourced from the existing _dd path; all pre-existing kernel/channel methods are behaviourally unchanged; delay_sep is the full-cluster (F008) minimum, not a real-only set; engine refusals (LensDomainError, CancellationError) propagate unswallowed.
  Max turns: 40

### WP2: Envelope-and-carrier reconstruction in the microlensed likelihood hot path
  What: Rewire `_amplification_coefficients` in likelihood.py to interpolate ONLY the smooth per-image envelopes at a config-independent coarse node count, then reconstruct the dense-frequency channel kernels K_a(w) analytically from carriers + smootherstep -- replacing the current direct interpolation of the oscillatory K_a. Return the identical (alpha, tau, K_dense) so the (k0,k1) reduction, _data_term, _norm_term, and LensedBinningError guard are unchanged.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/likelihood.py
  How: (1) Replace the coarse-node kernel evaluation with a call to `channels.transition_envelopes(w_coarse)`. Build w_coarse from a CONFIG-INDEPENDENT base `_ENVELOPE_NODES = 48` log-spaced nodes across the in-band w range, UNIONED with the existing regime/smootherstep/branch transition frequencies (the F008 real+virtual boundary set already assembled by `_coarse_w_node_grid`). The node count must NOT scale with beat-cycle count or any per-config oscillation measure -- 48 is a fixed constant (Professor's conservative Fresnel-scale bound; ~48*n_img*1us ~= 0.2ms engine, ample headroom). (2) Cubic-spline (not-a-knot, real and imag separately) each per-image envelope R_j from coarse to the dense bin sub-samples, reusing the existing spline machinery now applied to R_j instead of K_a. (3) Reconstruct at dense frequencies: K_a(w) = S(w)*R_a(w) + (1-S(w))*(1/alpha_a)*sum_j alpha_j*R_j(w)*exp(-i*phi_{a,j}(w)), where S(w)=smootherstep(w*delay_sep, 0.5, 4.0) is computed analytically (peel the switch OUT of the interpolated object; never interpolate through it), Delta_{a,j}=tau_j-tau_a, and phi_{a,j}(w)=mod(w*Delta_{a,j}, 2*pi) -- reduce mod 2*pi BEFORE the complex exp to avoid F001 large-phase precision loss (w*Delta reaches ~4000 rad on the crown). (4) Degenerate-carrier guard: when |Delta_{a,j}| < `_DELTA_MERGE_TOL = 1e-3` (dimensionless delay) treat the pair as a single DC carrier (phase == 0) and accumulate BY VALUE (sum the alpha_j*R_j contributions), NEVER by index -- handles image merging as Delta->0 near fold/cusp caustics without silent wrong cancellation. (5) Return (alpha, tau, K_dense) with the current method's exact shapes; make NO change to _data_term, _norm_term, the (k0,k1) reduction, _edge_linear_coefficients, the LensedBinningError guard, or lnlike_bruteforce. Keep reconstruction pure-numpy/vectorized -- add NO new njit (the only njit is the reused _dd path inside transition_envelopes). (6) Engine refusals must propagate unswallowed on BOTH the RB and brute paths exactly as before.
  Who: Coder
  Dependencies: WP1
  Verification: `_amplification_coefficients` builds the coarse grid from a fixed `_ENVELOPE_NODES=48` base unioned with the existing F008 boundary frequencies, interpolates per-image envelopes, and reconstructs dense K_a via analytic mod-2*pi carriers + peeled-out smootherstep with the `_DELTA_MERGE_TOL` degenerate-carrier by-value merge; the (alpha, tau, K_dense) return signature and all downstream contraction/reduction/guard code are unchanged; no per-config beat-cycle quantity appears in the node budget; no new njit is introduced; engine refusals propagate unswallowed on both RB and brute paths.
  Max turns: 75

### Professor Inputs
  - Decomposition is exact and obstruction-free: K_a(w) = S(w)*R_a(w) + (1-S(w))*(1/alpha_a)*sum_j alpha_j*R_j(w)*exp(-i*w*Delta_{a,j}); envelopes R_j are Fresnel-scale smooth and carriers hold ALL oscillation.
  - CODE-PINNED efficiency finding that reshapes the plan: the per-image residuals R_j come from `image_amplification_factor` -> `_dd_image` -> numba `_hyp1f1` (~1us/image/node), NOT F_op_grid (0.37ms/node). Corrected budget is ~3-5 ms warm with envelopes ALONE -- the surrogate and micro-levers are unnecessary for the 10 ms gate.
  - New API is a thin `transition_envelopes(w)` on ChangRefsdalChannels wrapping existing internal methods; no _gauge.py/operator.py/_dd.py change. Downstream _data_term/_norm_term/(k0,k1) consume the reconstructed K_a unchanged -- same (alpha, tau, K_dense) return signature.
  - Config-independent envelope node count is 32-48 (Fresnel-scale set), NOT the beat-cycle count; 48 recommended as a conservative fixed base. Config-independence (one constant works for all anchors) is the acceptance criterion.
  - Reference frame: per-channel tau_a^gauge is already what the code uses (the likelihood applies exp(-2pi*i*f*tau_a) per image); carriers use Delta_{a,j}=tau_j-tau_a^gauge -- no reference change needed.
  - Numerical risk (F001): w*Delta reaches ~4000 rad on the crown; reduce carrier phase mod 2pi BEFORE the complex exp. No risk to the F008 full-cluster switch rule or refusal symmetry, provided the carrier set is recomputed whenever the channel assignment changes and degenerate (Delta->0) carriers are merged to DC.
  - Test tolerances carry the Professor's authority: reconstruction/production interp gate 1e-3 null-safe; RB-vs-brute max(1.5, 1e-2|bf|); continuity 1e-6 across smootherstep edges; caustic-crossing |F| continuity ~1e-4; degenerate-carrier merge threshold at the point where max carrier phase over the band < ~1% cycle.
  - Honest step-rule read: envelopes alone should hit the ceiling, but the residual risk to watch is per-image _dd reconstruction fidelity in deep-unresolved near-caustic sub-bands -- the reconstruction-vs-exact_total gate across near-cusp/near-fold is the binding check; if a sub-band fails, gate at the derived floor and escalate that sub-band, do not widen tolerances.

### Domain Test Descriptions
  - ENVELOPE SMOOTHNESS + CONFIG-INDEPENDENT NODE COUNT. Setup: the five anchor configs from the Build 3d specs (crown, near-cusp, well-separated 2-image, near-fold, sheared small-w). For each, take a dense w grid (>=2000 pts) across the transition band. Operation: obtain the smooth per-image envelopes R_j via `ChangRefsdalChannels.transition_envelopes` on the dense grid; measure each envelope's oscillation content (zero-crossing count of Re(R_j) minus its smooth trend, and its dominant Fourier scale). Then interpolate R_j from the fixed 48-node config-independent coarse base and reconstruct K_a; compare to the dense-grid exact channel kernels. Expected: for ALL five configs the SAME 48-node base achieves max|K_recon - K_exact|/max(|K_exact|, floor) < 1e-3 (null-safe, floor as in the existing production gate); each envelope shows < 2 full oscillation cycles across the band; the passing node count does NOT scale with the per-config beat-cycle count (crown's ~9 cycles must not force more nodes than the 2-image config). Diagnostic: overlay Re/Im of R_j vs w (should be visibly smooth) and a bar chart of nodes-to-pass per config (should be flat at/under 48).
  - RECONSTRUCTION vs EXACT_TOTAL ACROSS THE FULL TRANSITION BAND (binding correctness gate; catches any near-caustic breakdown of the per-image _dd reconstruction). Setup: all five anchor configs, dense w grid spanning [0.8*w_lo, 1.2*w_hi] (into the pure resolved and pure unresolved regimes). Operation: reconstruct the total F(w) = sum_a alpha_a*K_a*exp(-i*w*tau_a) from the envelope+carrier scheme and compare to the engine's untouched `exact_total`/`_exact_total` on the same grid. Expected: max|F_recon - F_exact|/max(|F_exact|, floor) < 1e-3 (null-safe) for every config, INCLUDING deep-unresolved near-cusp and near-fold sub-bands. If any sub-band fails, that is the escalation trigger (step rule): report the failing w-range and config; do NOT widen the tolerance. Diagnostic: plot |F_recon - F_exact| vs w per config with the transition-band edges marked; the near-cusp/near-fold curves are the ones to watch.
  - RB LNLIKE vs BRUTE FORCE AT ORIGINAL GATES. Setup: each of the five anchor configs plus the crown injection (a concrete lensed CBC event; reuse the Build 3d/3b fixtures). Operation: evaluate the public `lnlike` (envelope path) and `lnlike_bruteforce` (untouched oracle) at fiducial params and at a spread of parameter-space points. Expected: |lnlike - lnlike_bruteforce| < max(1.5, 1e-2*|lnlike_bruteforce|) at every point and config -- the ORIGINAL RB-vs-brute gate, unchanged. Diagnostic: scatter of lnlike vs lnlike_bruteforce with the tolerance band; any outlier flags a reconstruction defect.
  - CONTINUITY ACROSS THE SMOOTHERSTEP BAND (no new discontinuities). Setup: crown and near-fold configs, dense w grid straddling both transition-band edges w_lo and w_hi. Operation: compute the reconstruction error |K_a_recon - K_a_exact| as a function of w. Expected: the error is continuous across w_lo and w_hi (no spike or jump at the smootherstep edges -- |error(edge+eps) - error(edge-eps)| below a tight bound, e.g. 1e-6, for eps ~ 0.01*edge), and the maximum error occurs in the band interior, not at the edges (a boundary spike would indicate mismatched carrier sets between regimes). Diagnostic: error-vs-w plot with edges annotated.
  - CAUSTIC-CROSSING LABEL/GAUGE CONTINUITY + DEGENERATE-CARRIER MERGE. Setup: a parametric family of lens configs sweeping source position across a caustic (4-image -> 2-image), so two images merge and Delta_{a,j} -> 0; build the crossing scenarios from geometry/operator/_gauge ONLY (F002 oracle-tautology guard: never import or derive ground truth from channels.py; enforce with the existing AST import-guard idiom). Operation: over the sweep, reconstruct total F(w) via the envelope scheme and compare to exact_total; track the carrier set as Delta->0. Expected: |F_recon - F_exact|/|F_exact| < 1e-3 at every sweep point including the crossing; as |Delta| falls below `_DELTA_MERGE_TOL`=1e-3 the pair is handled as a SINGLE DC carrier and contributions accumulate by value (no near-degenerate double-count, no discontinuity in |F| across the crossing beyond ~1e-4); the existing topology-stable channel-tracking / crossing-scenario tests remain green. Diagnostic: |F| vs sweep parameter (must be continuous) and a trace of active-carrier count across the crossing.
  - REFUSAL SYMMETRY UNDER THE ENVELOPE SCHEME. Setup: configs that trigger geometry.LensDomainError (macro-saddle / 1-kappa <= |gamma| boundary; use float64-exact boundary points per F004) and operator.CancellationError (an uncertifiable contraction in the F005 band). Operation: call both `lnlike` (envelope RB path) and `lnlike_bruteforce`. Expected: BOTH paths raise the SAME named exception, unswallowed, for the same inputs -- the certified-or-named-refusal contract survives the re-decomposition verbatim; no path silently returns nan or a finite-but-wrong value. Diagnostic: a table of (config -> exception type) for RB vs brute; any asymmetry is a failure.
  - MOD-2PI CARRIER PHASE-REDUCTION CORRECTNESS (guards F001 large-phase precision loss). Setup: a crown-scale case where w*Delta reaches thousands of radians. Operation: reconstruct the carrier contributions exp(-i*mod(w*Delta,2pi)) at dense frequencies and compare against a high-precision (e.g. mpmath or extended-accumulation) reference of exp(-i*w*Delta). Expected: agreement to ~1e-12 relative; a deliberately UNREDUCED float64 exp(-i*w*Delta) is shown to lose several digits at the largest w*Delta (mutation check demonstrating the reduction is load-bearing, i.e. removing it goes measurably worse). Diagnostic: |carrier_reduced - carrier_ref| and |carrier_unreduced - carrier_ref| vs w*Delta.
  - TIMING GATES (self-relative, arithmetic-derived; single self-consistent harness -- do NOT import absolute ms figures across harnesses). Structural-first: (a) node-count config-independence -- assert the passing envelope node count is the same fixed base for all five anchor configs and does not grow with beat-cycle count; (b) public-entry-point speedup floor -- `lnlike` faster than `lnlike_bruteforce` by a conservative margin measured in the same harness. Then the absolute ceiling: warm, thread-pinned, best-of-5 `lnlike` on the crown config <= 10 ms (HARD). Setup: warm the caches (first eval discarded), pin to a single thread, best-of-5. Expected: structural gates pass and the warm crown lnlike <= 10 ms; if the ceiling is missed for an unanticipated reason, record the measured floor and the dominant bottleneck (step rule -- escalate, do not widen). Diagnostic: per-component timing breakdown (transition_envelopes engine, spline, carrier application, contraction, non-engine overhead) so the bottleneck is named.
  - F010 py_func FALSIFIABILITY (only if any new njit is introduced -- the plan intends none). If WP2 unexpectedly adds njit code, expose `.py_func` on it and provide a self-falsification test that perturbs a load-bearing constant/branch and is SHOWN to go RED through the py_func chain (numba freezes module globals, so Python-level monkeypatching of compiled code is vacuous -- patch the entire call chain to py_func bodies). If no new njit is added, instead assert the reconstruction test still exercises the reused _dd/_hyp1f1 njit path (a mutation to a _dd input measurably changes the reconstructed kernel).

